<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alberta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alberta is a province of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-columbia">British Columbia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saskatchewan">Saskatchewan</a>, with Edmonton as its capital and Calgary as its largest city. Once part of Rupert's Land and the North-Western Territory, it became a province in 1905. Its economy rests on farming, ranching and, since the discovery at Leduc in 1947, oil and gas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alberta.jpg" alt="Alberta" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kooma (original) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Alberta.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
